{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":42.45000076293945,"text":"Look at Juctus from Heraklion, with the sun low. The line of the ridge makes a forehead, a nose, a mouth, and a beard, an enormous face lying on its back. The ancient Cretans said it was Zeus, and that Zeus was buried there. This annoyed the rest of the Greeks, because for them, Zeus never died, so they said the Cretans were liars. An entire argument between an island and a mainland, over a mountain that looks like a face. On its summit, at 811 meters, there was a Minoan sanctuary, one of those shrines that were not built in towns, but high up, in the open air. Today, Juctus is a protected area, and vultures ride the air above its slopes.","words":[{"word":"Look","start":0,"end":0.5},{"word":"at","start":0.5,"end":0.9599999785423279},{"word":"Juctus","start":0.9599999785423279,"end":1.0399999618530273},{"word":"from","start":1.0399999618530273,"end":1.659999966621399},{"word":"Heraklion","start":1.659999966621399,"end":2.240000009536743},{"word":"with","start":2.4800000190734863,"end":2.5999999046325684},{"word":"the","start":2.5999999046325684,"end":2.799999952316284},{"word":"sun","start":2.799999952316284,"end":3.0199999809265137},{"word":"low","start":3.0199999809265137,"end":3.4200000762939453},{"word":"The","start":4,"end":4.079999923706055},{"word":"line","start":4.079999923706055,"end":4.380000114440918},{"word":"of","start":4.380000114440918,"end":4.599999904632568},{"word":"the","start":4.599999904632568,"end":4.699999809265137},{"word":"ridge","start":4.699999809265137,"end":4.980000019073486},{"word":"makes","start":4.980000019073486,"end":5.260000228881836},{"word":"a","start":5.260000228881836,"end":5.619999885559082},{"word":"forehead","start":5.619999885559082,"end":5.900000095367432},{"word":"a","start":6.340000152587891,"end":6.860000133514404},{"word":"nose","start":6.860000133514404,"end":6.860000133514404},{"word":"a","start":7.179999828338623,"end":7.659999847412109}